# A Claude Code user relying on an installed plugin (rubber-ducky, from
# ~/.claude/plugins, which contributes only skills — no commands/agents/MCP
# in this install). Real HOME on purpose (not scratch): kiln has no plugin
# loader, so this checks whether anything from ~/.claude/plugins leaks
# through by accident, read-only.
@real
@size 140x45
@fixture qa/fixtures/real/ext-plugins

WAITFOR /describe a task/ 30
SEND /plugin
WAIT 1
SHOT plugin-command
TYPE /
WAIT 1
SHOT slash-palette
EXPECT_NOT /rubber-duck/
KEY backspace
TURN Use the rubber-duck skill to help me think through why our CI flakes about 1 in 20 runs (see notes.txt). Do not change any files, just talk it through.
SHOT rubber-duck-attempt
NOTE expected gap: kiln has no plugin support (/plugin prints marketplaces are unsupported, per docs/configuration.md); rubber-ducky's skills (~/.claude/plugins/cache/apato-plugins/rubber-ducky/1.0.0/skills/*) live outside the ~/.claude/skills and <cwd>/.claude/skills roots kiln actually reads, so none of them should appear in the palette and the TURN above should fall back to the model reasoning unaided, not an actual skill invocation.
